## 7. Booking state machine (UI and mock backend must enforce)

States: REQUESTED, NEEDS_INFORMATION, ELIGIBILITY_BLOCKED, PENDING_REVIEW, WAITLISTED, APPROVED, REJECTED, CANCELLED, CHECKED_OUT_TO_USER, RETURN_PENDING_CONFIRMATION, RETURNED, OVERDUE, CLOSED.

Transitions:
- REQUESTED -> PENDING_REVIEW | ELIGIBILITY_BLOCKED | CANCELLED
- PENDING_REVIEW -> APPROVED | REJECTED | WAITLISTED | NEEDS_INFORMATION
- WAITLISTED -> PENDING_REVIEW | APPROVED | CANCELLED
- APPROVED -> CANCELLED | CHECKED_OUT_TO_USER | OVERDUE
- CHECKED_OUT_TO_USER -> RETURN_PENDING_CONFIRMATION | RETURNED | OVERDUE
- RETURN_PENDING_CONFIRMATION -> RETURNED
- RETURNED -> CLOSED
The client never sets status directly; it calls action endpoints and renders the result. Invalid transitions return 400 and are shown as friendly messages.

